{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G model the robot's motion capabilities and perception outcomes as separate subsystems, ensuring modularity and composability. The specification automata E encode the safe exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, one-shot recovery turns. The supervisor never allows forward or random_walk actions when an obstacle is detected in front, and always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end recovery only. All automata are deterministic, total on uncontrollables, and avoid oscillatory or stalling behaviors.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion commands and perception events to allow flexible specification composition.",
    "Specification automata enforce safe, efficient exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward in progress, rotate on obstacle, and rapid return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
